# Project Kegel – Open-Source Ninepin Landmark Centre Blueprint

Building the future of ninepin bowling — one transparent step at a time.

We are creating a state-of-the-art, 6-lane ninepin bowling sports centre (with bar, training rooms, and community focus) as the world's first fully documented, copy-paste blueprint.  
The first centre will be founder-led with majority control for fast execution and fraud protection — but everything (designs, budgets, lessons, mistakes) is open-sourced under CC0 so anyone can fork this repo and build their own version anywhere in the world.

### Why This Project
Ninepin bowling (kegeln, kuglanje, quilles, kręgle...) has a passionate global community, especially in Europe. We want a modern, sustainable, accessible hub that preserves tradition while innovating — and we want the exact how-to public so more centres can follow.

### Core Principles
- Radical transparency — every euro tracked publicly on Open Collective.  
- Founder commitment — Bostjan Pen (25+ years in ninepin as playercoachpromoter) €200–300 monthly donations + minimum 10–15 hoursweek.  
- Governance — Heavy community advisory input, but the founder retains veto on core vision and major decisions (rationale always published for full accountability).  
- License — CC0 (public domain) — free to copy, adapt, use commercially or otherwise.

