### Facility v1 Spec (Copyable Baseline)

Core Concept  
A modern, sustainable, community-focused ninepin bowling hub designed for accessibility, low operating costs, and high social value. Built to prove the model in the first centre, then fully open-sourced for replication worldwide.


Ground Floor (Main Activity & Public Area)  
- 6 premium ninepin lanes equipped with modern string pinsetters (mandatory standard – e.g., Funk Bowling style or equivalent) 90%+ lower maintenance, 70%+ energy savings, minimal downtime, easier staffing.  
- Changing rooms with secure lockers.  
- Cozy bar (50–80 seats) – social hub for events, post-game gatherings, and casual visitors.  
- Pro shop – sales of ninepin equipment, apparel, and accessories.  
- Warmupmultipurpose area – space for stretching, dry training, or small events.

1st Floor (Training & Rental Spaces)  
- Multiple multipurposetraining rooms (e.g., 2–4 rooms) – rentable for workshops, team practices, other sportsyogafitness classes, meetings, or community events to generate additional revenue and broaden appeal.  
- Optional Small officeadmin space or viewing gallery overlooking the lanes (if layout allows).

Additional Features  
- Full accessibility (ramps, elevators if needed, inclusive design).  
- Sustainability built-in heat pump heatingcooling, solar-ready roof, energy-efficient lightinginsulation.  
- Target build cost (excluding plotland) €1.5M–€3M (realistic European range; lanesequipment ~€200–400k, constructionfit-out the rest). Adjust based on location and final feasibility study.

